<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">at the point <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. This is an algebraic equation, and we can write one for each point of our interest other than <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> (such as <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, etc.), thereby generating the said system of algebraic equations to be solved computationally.

For now, however, we would like to focus on finite difference approximations to derivatives alone, for doing so allows us to not only build a basis for our numerical methods later but also investigate several key concepts, such as the order of accuracy of an approximation in the simplest possible setting.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">First order derivatives</Text-field></Title><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We will first look at first order derivatives. An obvious choice (given the example above especially) for a finite difference approximation is the following.</Text-field>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L23" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">d[p](u(conjugate(x))) := (u(conjugate(x)+h)-u(conjugate(x)))/h;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+LSZJImRHRig2I0kicEdGKDYjLUkidUdGKDYjLUkqY29uanVnYXRlR0YmNiNJInhHRigqJiwmLUY0NiMsJkY2IiIiSSJoR0YoRj9GP0YzISIiRj9GQEZBNyNGOg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L26" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">As the reader might have guessed, another possible choice is</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L27" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">d[m](u(conjugate(x))) := (u(conjugate(x))-u(conjugate(x)-h))/h;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+LSZJImRHRig2I0kibUdGKDYjLUkidUdGKDYjLUkqY29uanVnYXRlR0YmNiNJInhHRigqJiwmRjMiIiItRjQ2IywmRjZGPEkiaEdGKCEiIkZBRjxGQEZBNyNGOg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L29" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Note that we have assumed <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> to be positive here, and we will always assume this to be the case. Both<Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and<Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> are known as one-sided approximations as they use values of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEidUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEidUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> at <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> values that are all either<Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> or <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, and they both are first order accurate approximations. For now, take this to just mean that the error in these approximations (which would be defined as either <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> or <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>) is proportional to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> approximately.

Another possibility is to use the so-called centered approximation</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L30" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">d[0](u(conjugate(x))) := (u(conjugate(x)+h)-u(conjugate(x)-h))/(2*h);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+LSZJImRHRig2IyIiITYjLUkidUdGKDYjLUkqY29uanVnYXRlR0YmNiNJInhHRigsJComLCYtRjQ2IywmRjYiIiJJImhHRihGQEZALUY0NiMsJkY2RkBGQSEiIkZFRkBGQUZFI0ZAIiIjNyNGOg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L33" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">which could be rewritten as the average of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> as well:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L34" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">d[0](u(conjugate(x))) := (d[p](u(conjugate(x)))+d[m](u(conjugate(x))))/2;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+LSZJImRHRig2IyIiITYjLUkidUdGKDYjLUkqY29uanVnYXRlR0YmNiNJInhHRigsJiomLCYtRjQ2IywmRjYiIiJJImhHRihGQEZARjMhIiJGQEZBRkIjRkAiIiMqJiwmRjNGQC1GNDYjLCZGNkZARkFGQkZCRkBGQUZCRkM3I0Y6</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L36" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This is a second-order approximation, meaning that the error is roughly proportional to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1cEdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtSSNtbkdGJDYlUSIyRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRidGMkY1RjgvJTFzdXBlcnNjcmlwdHNoaWZ0R1EiMEYnRjVGQQ==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1cEdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtSSNtbkdGJDYlUSIyRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRidGMkY1RjgvJTFzdXBlcnNjcmlwdHNoaWZ0R1EiMEYnRjVGQQ==</Equation>. The finite difference approximations to the first derivative presented so far are all pretty intuitive. However, other approximations are also possible that are both extremely nonintuitive and more accurate. An example would be</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L37" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">d[3](u(conjugate(x))) := (2*u(conjugate(x)+h)+3*u(conjugate(x))-6*u(conjugate(x)-h)+u(conjugate(x)-2*h))/(6*h);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+LSZJImRHRig2IyIiJDYjLUkidUdGKDYjLUkqY29uanVnYXRlR0YmNiNJInhHRigsJComLCotRjQ2IywmRjYiIiJJImhHRihGQCIiI0YzRjEtRjQ2IywmRjZGQEZBISIiISInLUY0NiMsJkY2RkBGQSEiI0ZARkBGQUZGI0ZAIiInNyNGOg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L39" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">which is a third order approximation. Our goal is to develop a systematic way to derive such formulas and analyze their accuracy.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Errors</Text-field></Title><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The standard approach to analyzing the error in a finite difference approximation is to expand each of the function values of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEidUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEidUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> in a Taylor series about <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L44" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq1 := u(conjugate(x)+h) = series(u(conjugate(x)+h), h, 5);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L45" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq2 := u(conjugate(x)-h) = series(u(conjugate(x)-h), h, 5);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L47" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Using these, we see that</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L48" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq3 := d[p](u(conjugate(x))) = subs(eq1, d[p](u(conjugate(x))));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L53" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">or</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L54" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq3a := d[p](u(conjugate(x))) = series(simplify(subs(convert(eq1, polynom), d[p](u(conjugate(x))))), h, 1);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVlcTNhR0YoLyomLCYtSSJ1R0YoNiMsJi1JKmNvbmp1Z2F0ZUdGJjYjSSJ4R0YoIiIiSSJoR0YoRjlGOS1GMjYjRjUhIiJGOUY6Rj0rJ0Y6LS1JIkRHRiU2I0YyRjwiIiEtSSJPR0YlNiNGOUY5NyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L52" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Similarly,</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L55" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq4 := d[m](u(conjugate(x))) = subs(eq2, d[m](u(conjugate(x))));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L57" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">or</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L58" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq4a := d[m](u(conjugate(x))) = series(simplify(subs(convert(eq2, polynom), d[m](u(conjugate(x))))), h, 1);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVlcTRhR0YoLyomLCYtSSJ1R0YoNiMtSSpjb25qdWdhdGVHRiY2I0kieEdGKCIiIi1GMjYjLCZGNEY4SSJoR0YoISIiRj1GOEY8Rj0rJ0Y8LS1JIkRHRiU2I0YyRjMiIiEtSSJPR0YlNiNGOEY4NyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L60" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Combining the Taylor expansions for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, we could get the expansion for the centered approximation:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L62" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq5 := subs({eq1, eq2}, d[0](u(conjugate(x))));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L64" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">or</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L65" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq5a := series(simplify(subs({convert(eq1, polynom), convert(eq2, polynom)}, d[0](u(conjugate(x))))), h, 2);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVlcTVhR0YoKydJImhHRigtLUkiREdGJTYjSSJ1R0YoNiMtSSpjb25qdWdhdGVHRiY2I0kieEdGKCIiIS1JIk9HRiU2IyIiIiIiIzcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L67" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Calculating the Taylor expansion of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> about <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, we get</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L69" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq6 := u(conjugate(x)-2*h) = series(u(conjugate(x)-2*h), h, 5);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L71" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This allows us to show that</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L72" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq6a := d[3](u(conjugate(x))) = series(simplify(subs({convert(eq1, polynom), convert(eq2, polynom), convert(eq6, polynom)}, d[3](u(conjugate(x))))), h, 3);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Deriving finite difference approximations</Text-field></Title><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Suppose we want to derive a finite difference approximation to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> based on some given set of points. We can use Taylor series to derive an appropriate formula, using the method of undetermined coefficients.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Suppose we want a one-sided approximation to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> based on <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, and <Equation executable="true" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> of the form</Text-field>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L83" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">d[2](u(conjugate(x))) := a*u(conjugate(x))+b*u(conjugate(x)-h)+c*u(conjugate(x)-2*h);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+LSZJImRHRig2IyIiIzYjLUkidUdGKDYjLUkqY29uanVnYXRlR0YmNiNJInhHRigsKComSSJhR0YoIiIiRjNGPUY9KiZJImJHRihGPS1GNDYjLCZGNkY9SSJoR0YoISIiRj1GPSomSSJjR0YoRj0tRjQ2IywmRjZGPUZDISIjRj1GPTcjRjo=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L85" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Taylor expansion gets us</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L86" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
