<Group labelreference="L124" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Whereas the former is an uncentered approximation to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, the latter is a centered one. Another way to derive finite difference approximations to higher order derivatives is the generalized method of undetermined coefficients. We want an approximation to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> based on <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> points <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation><Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation><Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUwZm9udF9zdHlsZV9uYW1lR1EpMkR+SW5wdXRGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRictRiM2JC1GLzYmUSJuRidGMkY1RjgvRjlRJ25vcm1hbEYnLyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGQA==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYkLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUwZm9udF9zdHlsZV9uYW1lR1EpMkR+SW5wdXRGJy8lLG1hdGh2YXJpYW50R1EnaXRhbGljRictRiM2JC1GLzYmUSJuRidGMkY1RjgvRjlRJ25vcm1hbEYnLyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGQA==</Equation>. The linear combination <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> should agree with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>as well as possible. We Taylor expand each of the <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> about <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JVEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdpdGFsaWNGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnL0YzUSdub3JtYWxGJw==</Equation> and choose the coefficients <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> such that <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> if <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> otherwise for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. Provided the points <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> are distinct, this <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> Vandermonde system is nonsingular and has a unique solution.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L126" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">n := 4;k := 1;xs := [1, 0, -1, -2];fda := proc(n, k, xs)    local h, expr, i, exsr, sys, sol:    if verify(nops(xs), n, equal) then:        expr := 0;
        for i from 1 to n do:
            expr := expr+c[i]*u(x+xs[i]*h):
        od:        exsr := convert(series(expr, h, n), polynom);        for i from 1 to n do:
            if verify(i, k+1, equal) then:
                sys[i] := coeff(exsr, (D@@(i-1))(u)(x)) = 1:
            else:
                sys[i] := coeff(exsr, (D@@(i-1))(u)(x)) = 0:
            fi:
        od:        sys := convert(sys, set);
        sol := solve(sys, {seq(c[i], i = 1..n)});        subs(sol, expr):    else:        print(`Please enter an appropriate number of distinct points.`):    fi:end proc:    </Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJuR0YoIiIlNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJrR0YoIiIiNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSN4c0dGKDcmIiIiIiIhISIiISIjNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L127" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">appr := fda(n, k, xs);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
